    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras are positioned for a high-ceiling offensive output tonight, led by the elite efficiency of **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.12). His start against McGreevy provides the day\u2019s premier matchup; between his dynamic platoon advantage and the premium leadoff spot, he is the engine of today's lineup. He is closely followed by **Yordan Alvarez** (70.43) and **Lars Nootbaar** (67.77). **Yordan Alvarez** remains a cornerstone despite a neutral platoon, as his elite .464 xwOBA renders him matchup-proof, while **Lars Nootbaar** benefits significantly from a favorable SP_xERA of 4.65 and a strategic shift into the leadoff role. **Junior Caminero** (67.57) and **Kyle Schwarber** (65.94) round out our top-tier threats, providing the power profile necessary to capitalize on their respective favorable matchups.\n\nWe are navigating a few tactical hurdles, specifically regarding our lineup structure and the scarcity of stolen bases. While **Trea Turner** (62.60) carries a strong efficiency score, his upside is slightly capped by Prielipp's ability to hold runners, a specific constraint we monitor given the league\u2019s emphasis on SB velocity. The bench decision for **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (43.86) was the most difficult; while he provides an interesting power profile, he was ultimately pushed out by the higher floor provided by **Chase Meidroth** and **Caleb Durbin**. **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** remains our primary pivot should any of our late-slot starters like **Pedro Ramirez** be scratched. Please note that several spots remain \"Lineup Pending\"\u2014specifically for **Gary Sanchez**, **Trea Turner**, **Caleb Durbin**, **Christian Yelich**, and **Kyle Schwarber**\u2014meaning these projections assume historical order; any significant movement down the batting order for **Gary Sanchez** or **Christian Yelich** may necessitate a re-evaluation of their utility.",
